# Two interacting tanks: a pump fills tank 1, which drains into tank 2 through an
# orifice, and tank 2 drains to the open. Efforts are heads (m) and flows m^3/s;
# an orifice passes a*sqrt(2*g*h) for a head difference h, either way round.
# It settles where Q_in = a2*sqrt(2*g*h2) = a12*sqrt(2*g*(h1 - h2)). The tanks start
# part full: at zero head an orifice's law has an infinite slope, where the
# simulation can't start.

junction tank1 0: Qin-, T1+
junction mid 1: O12+
junction tank2 0: T2+, O2+

element Qin Sf value=Q_in
element T1 C C=A1
element O12 R f=Piecewise((a12*sqrt(2*g*e),e>0),(-a12*sqrt(-2*g*e),True))
element T2 C C=A2
element O2 R f=Piecewise((a2*sqrt(2*g*e),e>0),(-a2*sqrt(-2*g*e),True))
element bond3 TF n=1  # plain bond tank1 -> mid
element bond5 TF n=1  # plain bond mid -> tank2
connect bond3 tank1 mid
connect bond5 mid tank2

output h1 = e_T1
output h2 = e_T2
output Q_out = f_O2

# --- editor data (comments; bondgraph.py ignores these) ---
#@title Two tanks with orifices (nonlinear R)
#@pos Qin 90 240
#@pos tank1 260 240
#@pos T1 260 100
#@pos mid 430 240
#@pos O12 430 380
#@pos tank2 600 240
#@pos T2 600 100
#@pos O2 770 240
#@param Q_in=0.02
#@param A1=1
#@param A2=0.5
#@param a12=0.01
#@param a2=0.008
#@param g=9.81
#@init q_T1=0.2
#@init q_T2=0.05
#@sim tEnd=300 steps=3000
